/*
 * Main SRAM is split in two so the process memory pool has a fixed
 * home of its own.
 *
 * progbase used to be an ordinary BSS array: the linker placed it
 * after whatever the kernel happened to contain, so every build that
 * changed the kernel's size silently moved every process image.  That
 * corrupted user memory in ways that looked like application bugs.
 *
 * RAM holds the kernel and nothing else; PROGPOOL is exactly USERMEM
 * and runs to the top of main SRAM, where the scratch banks begin.
 * If the kernel outgrows its half the link now fails with "region RAM
 * overflowed" instead of quietly relocating user memory.
 *
 * Main SRAM is 512K and this split uses ALL of it: RAM + PROGPOOL is
 * exactly 0x80000.  There is no slack anywhere, so the two numbers
 * below only ever move against each other.
 *
 * The kernel took 4K once, when it had 192K and filled it, and another
 * 4K here for the text primitives - drawing a glyph at a pixel position
 * and the shared scroll (display_gfx_text, display_gfx_scroll), which
 * are what MMBasic's TEXT command and a graphics-mode PRINT are built
 * from.  The kernel is PICO_COPY_TO_RAM, so code costs RAM, and it was
 * 184 bytes short.
 *
 * What it costs a process: the largest goes from about 264K to 260K.
 * (The cap is "leave room for the biggest neighbour to be resident" -
 * largest_neighbour() in swapper.c - not PROGSIZE, which is now the
 * whole pool.)
 *
 * THE REAL FIX, when someone has time for it: .text is 90,676 bytes and
 * every one of them is copied into RAM at boot, while flash sits at
 * 115K of 512K used.  Dropping PICO_COPY_TO_RAM and marking only the
 * scanout and interrupt paths __not_in_flash_func() - the SDK's normal
 * idiom, and what MMBasic's own firmware does - would give back tens of
 * kilobytes rather than the four scraped together here.  It needs
 * measuring first: core1 renders each scanline on a deadline, and flash
 * shares the QMI with the PSRAM that holds the framebuffer layer and
 * bcrun's heap, so kernel cache misses would contend with them.
 *
 * KEEP THIS IN STEP WITH TOTALMEM in the Makefile: config.h sizes
 * progbase[] from USERMEM and the two must describe the same region.
 * Nothing checks that they agree.
 */
MEMORY
{
    RAM(rwx)     : ORIGIN = RAM_ORIGIN,           LENGTH = 0x33000
    PROGPOOL(rw) : ORIGIN = RAM_ORIGIN + 0x33000, LENGTH = 308k
}
